      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T01:50:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of adding these deps here and adding tool_path, could you add the tools to the `data` property of `apex_elf_checker` instead of `required`? This will bundle them into the `apex_elf_checker` tool, and you can extract them at runtime with python\u0027s `importlib.resources`.",
      "revId": "6f21a5033a6a0b2f94e1b43a846035573bed1a33",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c5ff228_c8cde3c0",
        "filename": "apex/builder.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 245,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T02:05:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, as a build time checker, I thought relying on external tools would be more efficient. (save cpu cycles, storage, etc).\n\nBtw, I see that bundling them in a python binary makes sense. I have a few questions:\n- what about other tools like deapexer? apex_elf_checker relies on deapexer which, in turn, relies on debugfs and others. would it make sense if deapexer bundles its dependencies?\n- what about shared libraries of other tools? For example, llvm-readelf uses libc++, libpthread, etc. Should apex_elf_checker bundle them as well?",
      "parentUuid": "c137b21f_df0d4709",
      "revId": "6f21a5033a6a0b2f94e1b43a846035573bed1a33",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "91a9733b_c9c2e7cd",
        "filename": "apex/builder.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 245,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T02:15:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yeah it is a tradeoff of some performance for a simpler build. Bazel has a \"runfiles\" feature that makes runtime dependencies clearer, we should probably have something like that in soong eventually too. Performance is not critical in this case because it\u0027s a validation action, but it may be worth checking and seeing if this change makes it drastically worse.\n\nIt would certainly make deapexer easier to use if it also bundled its tools.\n\nYeah shared libraries are annoying in soong. Using statically compiled tools simplifies this. But this current solution also doesn\u0027t handle shared libraries, so not bundling them into the python tool wouldn\u0027t be any different.",
      "parentUuid": "4c5ff228_c8cde3c0",
      "revId": "6f21a5033a6a0b2f94e1b43a846035573bed1a33",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
